{
  "info": {
    "name": "toy-mcp",
    "description": "Requests for the two toy MCP servers of the toy-mcp repository: a server built on v1 of the official TypeScript SDK, for protocol 2025-11-25, and a hand-written server for protocol 2026-07-28. One folder per server.\n\nStart the server a folder talks to before sending its requests, from the repository root:\n\n- `npm start` for the SDK server, at `http://127.0.0.1:3333/mcp`\n- `npm run start:2026` for the hand-written server, at `http://127.0.0.1:3334/mcp`\n\nThe collection variables `sdk` and `s2026` hold those two URLs. If you start a server on another port (for example `PORT=4000 npm start`), change the matching variable. The third variable, `jobId`, is set by the script on the `start_job` request; if it stays empty, paste the `jobId` from a `start_job` reply into it.\n\nSend the requests of a folder from top to bottom. Each name ends with what to expect: the HTTP status and, for a failure, the JSON-RPC error code or `isError`. No environment and no authorization are needed.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "SDK server :3333 (protocol 2025-11-25)",
      "description": "Version 1 of the official TypeScript SDK (`@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`) in stateless mode. Start it with `npm start`.\n\nEvery reply in this folder is HTTP 200 with an SSE frame, even for a single response: the JSON-RPC message is on the `data:` line. A problem with a tool call comes back as a result with `isError: true`. A problem with the protocol comes back as a JSON-RPC `error`.\n\nBoth headers are required. The SDK answers 406 without `Accept: application/json, text/event-stream` and 415 without `Content-Type: application/json`.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "initialize (old handshake) -> 200",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"method\": \"initialize\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"protocolVersion\": \"2025-11-25\",\n    \"capabilities\": {},\n    \"clientInfo\": {\n      \"name\": \"postman\",\n      \"version\": \"0\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{sdk}}",
              "host": [
                "{{sdk}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The handshake of the 2025 protocol. The reply carries `protocolVersion`, `capabilities` and `serverInfo`. No `Mcp-Session-Id` response header comes back, because the server runs in stateless mode."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "tools/list -> 200",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 2,\n  \"method\": \"tools/list\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{sdk}}",
              "host": [
                "{{sdk}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Lists the five tools with the JSON Schema of their inputs. It works without a prior `initialize`, because the server keeps no session."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "echo - ok -> 200",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"echo\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"text\": \"hello\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{sdk}}",
              "host": [
                "{{sdk}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The minimal tool call. The result is an array of typed content blocks, here one text block holding `hello`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "echo - wrong type -> 200 isError",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"echo\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"text\": 5\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{sdk}}",
              "host": [
                "{{sdk}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "`text` is a number. The SDK validates the arguments before the tool runs and answers with a normal result marked `isError: true`. The text names the failing field (`at text`)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "unknown tool -> 200 isError",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"nope\",\n    \"arguments\": {}\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{sdk}}",
              "host": [
                "{{sdk}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "A tool that does not exist. The answer has the same shape as a validation failure: a result with `isError: true` (`Tool nope not found`), not a JSON-RPC error."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "search_catalog -> 200",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"search_catalog\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"query\": \"\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{sdk}}",
              "host": [
                "{{sdk}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Step one of the marketplace pattern: find out what exists. An empty `query` returns all three items with their price and input fields. Set `query` to `report` to narrow it to one item."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "call_item - ok -> 200",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"call_item\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"item\": \"demo/hn-top\",\n      \"input\": {\n        \"mode\": \"top\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{sdk}}",
              "host": [
                "{{sdk}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Step two of the marketplace pattern: one generic tool runs any item. The reply shows the input after defaults were applied (`maxResults: 10`) and the price charged."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "call_item - two bad fields named -> 200 isError",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"call_item\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"item\": \"demo/hn-top\",\n      \"input\": {\n        \"mode\": \"trending\",\n        \"maxResults\": 500\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{sdk}}",
              "host": [
                "{{sdk}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "A bad enum value and a number out of range. Both fields are named in one reply (`input.mode` and `input.maxResults`), so a caller can fix the whole input in one retry."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "start_job (send twice: deduplicated) -> 200",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "// The reply is an SSE frame. The JSON-RPC message is on the data: line, and the tool's",
                  "// answer is a JSON string inside result.content[0].text.",
                  "const dataLine = pm.response.text().split('\\n').find((line) => line.startsWith('data: '));",
                  "if (dataLine) {",
                  "  const result = JSON.parse(dataLine.slice('data: '.length)).result;",
                  "  if (result && !result.isError) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('jobId', JSON.parse(result.content[0].text).jobId);",
                  "  }",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"start_job\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"item\": \"demo/slow-report\",\n      \"input\": {\n        \"topic\": \"mcp\"\n      },\n      \"idempotencyKey\": \"k-1\",\n      \"maxCostUsd\": 0.05\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{sdk}}",
              "host": [
                "{{sdk}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Starts a long-running item and returns a `jobId` handle instead of holding a session open. Send it twice: the second reply carries the same `jobId` with `deduplicated: true`, because the `idempotencyKey` is the same.\n\nThe script on this request copies the `jobId` into the `jobId` collection variable for `get_result`. The server remembers a key until it restarts, so a first reply that already says `deduplicated: true` means `k-1` was used earlier."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "start_job - over budget -> 200 isError",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"start_job\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"item\": \"demo/slow-report\",\n      \"input\": {\n        \"topic\": \"mcp\"\n      },\n      \"idempotencyKey\": \"k-2\",\n      \"maxCostUsd\": 0.001\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{sdk}}",
              "host": [
                "{{sdk}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "`maxCostUsd` is below the price of the item (0.01 USD), so the job is refused before any work starts."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "get_result (uses {{jobId}}) -> 200",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"get_result\",\n    \"arguments\": {\n      \"jobId\": \"{{jobId}}\"\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{sdk}}",
              "host": [
                "{{sdk}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Reads a job by its handle, taken from the `jobId` collection variable. For three seconds after `start_job` the state is `running`; after that it is `succeeded` and carries the result.\n\nAn empty or unknown `jobId` gets `No job ...` with `isError: true`. A valid id gets the same answer after the server restarts, because jobs live in memory."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "server/discover (not in SDK v1) -> 200 -32601",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 3,\n  \"method\": \"server/discover\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{sdk}}",
              "host": [
                "{{sdk}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The method that replaces `initialize` in the 2026-07-28 revision. Version 1 of the SDK does not implement that revision and answers with the JSON-RPC error `-32601` inside an HTTP 200. Compare request A in the other folder, where the same method is answered, and request H, where an unknown method is an HTTP 404."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Hand-written server :3334 (protocol 2026-07-28)",
      "description": "Node's `http` module only, for the 2026-07-28 revision. Start it with `npm run start:2026`. JSON-RPC replies are plain JSON, not SSE frames.\n\nA is the valid request. B to L are each answered with an error, and the name ends with the HTTP status and, where there is one, the JSON-RPC error code that comes back.\n\nA valid request carries the `MCP-Protocol-Version` and `Mcp-Method` headers (plus `Mcp-Name` for `tools/call`, `resources/read` and `prompts/get`), and `params._meta` with the protocol version and the client capabilities.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "A  discover - valid -> 200",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              },
              {
                "key": "MCP-Protocol-Version",
                "value": "2026-07-28"
              },
              {
                "key": "Mcp-Method",
                "value": "server/discover"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": \"d1\",\n  \"method\": \"server/discover\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"_meta\": {\n      \"io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion\": \"2026-07-28\",\n      \"io.modelcontextprotocol/clientCapabilities\": {}\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{s2026}}",
              "host": [
                "{{s2026}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The discovery call that replaces the `initialize` handshake. The reply lists `supportedVersions` and `capabilities`, names the server under `_meta`, and carries `ttlMs` and `cacheScope` so a client can cache it."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "B  discover - no MCP headers, no params -> 400 -32020",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": \"d2\",\n  \"method\": \"server/discover\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{s2026}}",
              "host": [
                "{{s2026}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Only `Content-Type` and `Accept` are sent: no `MCP-Protocol-Version` header, no `Mcp-Method` header and no `params`. The header check runs first, so the answer is `-32020` and not the `-32602` of request C."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "C  discover - headers ok, no _meta -> 400 -32602",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              },
              {
                "key": "MCP-Protocol-Version",
                "value": "2026-07-28"
              },
              {
                "key": "Mcp-Method",
                "value": "server/discover"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": \"d3\",\n  \"method\": \"server/discover\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{s2026}}",
              "host": [
                "{{s2026}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The headers are right but `params._meta` is missing. That is a malformed request: `-32602`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "D  header version != _meta -> 400 -32020",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              },
              {
                "key": "MCP-Protocol-Version",
                "value": "2025-11-25"
              },
              {
                "key": "Mcp-Method",
                "value": "server/discover"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": \"d4\",\n  \"method\": \"server/discover\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"_meta\": {\n      \"io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion\": \"2026-07-28\",\n      \"io.modelcontextprotocol/clientCapabilities\": {}\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{s2026}}",
              "host": [
                "{{s2026}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The header says `2025-11-25` and `_meta` says `2026-07-28`. The request contradicts itself: `-32020`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "E  version 1900-01-01 in both -> 400 -32022",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              },
              {
                "key": "MCP-Protocol-Version",
                "value": "1900-01-01"
              },
              {
                "key": "Mcp-Method",
                "value": "server/discover"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": \"d5\",\n  \"method\": \"server/discover\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"_meta\": {\n      \"io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion\": \"1900-01-01\",\n      \"io.modelcontextprotocol/clientCapabilities\": {}\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{s2026}}",
              "host": [
                "{{s2026}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The header and `_meta` agree on a version the server does not speak. `error.data` lists `supported` and `requested`, so a client knows what to retry with."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "F  Mcp-Method mismatch -> 400 -32020",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              },
              {
                "key": "MCP-Protocol-Version",
                "value": "2026-07-28"
              },
              {
                "key": "Mcp-Method",
                "value": "tools/list"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": \"d6\",\n  \"method\": \"server/discover\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"_meta\": {\n      \"io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion\": \"2026-07-28\",\n      \"io.modelcontextprotocol/clientCapabilities\": {}\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{s2026}}",
              "host": [
                "{{s2026}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The `Mcp-Method` header says `tools/list` and the body says `server/discover`: `-32020`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "G  tools/call Mcp-Name mismatch -> 400 -32020",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json, text/event-stream"
              },
              {
                "key": "MCP-Protocol-Version",
                "value": "2026-07-28"
              },
              {
                "key": "Mcp-Method",
                "value": "tools/call"
              },
              {
                "key": "Mcp-Name",
                "value": "foo"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\",\n  \"id\": 7,\n  \"method\": \"tools/call\",\n  \"params\": {\n    \"name\": \"bar\",\n    \"arguments\": {},\n    \"_meta\": {\n      \"io.modelcontextprotocol/protocolVersion\": \"2026-07-28\",\n      \"io.modelcontextprotocol/clientCapabilities\": {}\n    }\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{s2026}}",
              "host": [
                "{{s2026}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "For `tools/call` the `Mcp-Name` header must equal `params.name`. Here the header says `foo` and the body says `bar`: `-32020`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "H  resources/read valid -> 404 -32601",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
